# Shared environment for the three MyGO Fighter services.
# Installed as /etc/mygo-fighter/base.env (root:mygo, mode 0640) and read by
# mygo-edge, mygo-lobby and mygo-rooms@.service.
#
# INTERNAL_SECRET authenticates service-to-service calls. install.sh appends a
# generated 64-character hexadecimal value when this file has no active
# INTERNAL_SECRET line. Every role must use the same value; change it in this
# file only, then restart all three units.
# INTERNAL_SECRET=

# Rooms instances owned by this host. activate.sh and rollback.sh start/stop
# these instances and install.sh enables their template units. IDs must match
# [a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*; each instance needs a free ROOMS_PORT. The default public
# layout uses one instance ("a", port 8091). For a second instance, add it here
# and create /etc/mygo-fighter/rooms-<id>.env with ROOMS_PORT=8092.
ROOMS_INSTANCES="a"
